# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing below this heading may ever reach a public remote. Each pattern is
# narrow on purpose: a broad one hides a legitimate file without saying so.

# Environment files. The example is tracked so a reader knows which keys exist.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Registry and network credentials. `.npmrc` holds the npm publish token, and
# this package is published, so it is the most likely thing to leak from here.
.npmrc
.netrc
_netrc

# Private keys and certificate bundles.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*

# Cloud and CI credential files.
credentials.json
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json
.aws/
.gcloud/

# A .gitignore only stops an untracked file. It does not stop `git add -f`, and
# it does nothing for a file that is already tracked or already in history.

# ── ADDONE state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Intent, contracts, rules, decisions and scopes stay tracked. Only derived
# state is ignored.
.addone/.cache/

# Local-only architecture state, for anyone who opts out of tracked sidecar mode.
.addone.local/

# ── Agent hosts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code worktree scratch. This becomes wrong the day `addone init` lands:
# init writes `.claude/settings.json` into a target repo and that file is meant
# to be tracked. Narrow this to the scratch paths when that ticket ships.
.claude/

# Every host's local override, which is where a per-machine token would sit.
*.local.json

# ── Build and editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
prototypes/**/out/
.DS_Store
*.swp
